-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",4,{
[97]="700583DB\n1\tTalk to Náth at Zudramdân\tZudramdân can be found in Elderslade. You should talk to Náth at Zudramdân.\n2\tRally for war at the banner of Gabil'akkâ\tThe rally banner of Gabil'akkâ can be found at Zudramdân in Elderslade. You should rally for war at the banner of Gabil'akkâ.\n3\tTalk to Agátur the Boastful at Zarkul-sulûn\030Talk to Náth at Zarkul-sulûn\030Talk to Rúzat at Zarkul-sulûn\tAgátur the Boastful, Náth, and Rúzat have all joined the War of Three Peaks. You should talk to Agátur the Boastful, Náth, and Rúzat at Zarkul-sulûn.\n4\tAssist Gloin with 'Into the Fray'\030Assist Rísti Graver with 'Strength and Fury'\030Assist Rísti Graver with 'The Tamers of Howlers' Notch'\030Assist Náin the Slakeless with 'The Commander of Zudramdân'\tThere is much to be done in times of war. You should assist the dwarves in the War of Three Peaks.\n5\tTalk to Agátur the Boastful at Zarkul-sulûn\tAgátur the Boastful can be found at Zarkul-sulûn. You should talk to Agátur the Boastful at Zarkul-sulûn.\n6\tTalk to Stálskeg Ironbeard\tStálskeg Ironbeard can be found at Annâk-khurfu. You should talk to Stálskeg Ironbeard to continue assisting the Gabil'akkâ.\n",
[98]="7000D3D0\n1\tTalk to Branan\tBranan is by the front-gate of the city of Donnvail, north-east of Fail-á-Khro. Una has told you that your allies can aid her in the struggle against Angmar, but if your allies are not near at hand, you can still aid her by bringing a message to Branan.\n2\tTalk to Crannog\tCrannog is at his ruling-seat west of the central island in Aughaire, south of Fail-á-Khro. Una and Branan have come to the conclusion that the time to rise against their Angmarim masters has almost arrived, and Crannog should be petitioned for aid in the effort.\n",
[99]="70062CE3\n1\tRosentyl Flutch has asked you to let her children know that it is time to eat. Rosentyl's children can be found around Clegur.\t\n2\tReturn to Rosentyl\tRosentyl is in Clegur. You should let Rosentyl know that you have told all of her children to come enjoy the meal she has cooked.\n",
[100]="70049265\n1\tDestroy Orc tents in Dor Amarth (total: 10)\tOrcs encampments can be found around Dor Amarth. You should destroy any Orc tents that you find.\n2\tCompleted\tDestroyed many Orc tents in Dor Amarth.\n",
[101]="7006B079\n1\tSpeak with Khôltekh about his plan\tSpeak with Khôltekh about his plan.\n2\tMove over to the right of the group of archivists\tMove over to the right of the group of archivists.\n3\tDefeat false archivists (total: 3)\tDefeat the false archivists!\n4\tSpeak with Khôltekh\tSpeak with Khôltekh.\n",
[102]="7002ADDD\n1\tFind a cap in Winter-home\030Find a pipe near one of the tables in Winter-home\030Find an acorn below nearby trees\030Find a carrot near the chicken coops\030Gather coal near the servants' oven\030Gather sticks from nearby bushes (total: 2)\tThe materials you need to replicate Virgil's snowman can be found around Frostbluff. In order to replicate Virgil's snowman, you will need to gather the right materials.\n2\tBuild a cap-wearing snowman\tThe snowman-field is outside of Winter-home. Now that you have gathered all of the necessary supplies, you should return to the field and find a snowpile to build your snowman.\n",
[103]="70060FB5\n1\tScout a side window to 8 Honeymead Lane\tDinodas has his eye set on a side window through which you might be able to secretly gain access to 8 Honeymead Lane in order to steal back the gift.\n2\tTake a crate from the stack outside the Fox and Fiddle, in Nobottle\tThere are so many nosey hobbits around that you will need to stack crates outside the side entrance if you are to hide your caper from their view.\n3\tTake a crate from the stack outside the Fox and Fiddle, in Nobottle\tThere are so many nosey hobbits around that you will need to stack crates outside the side entrance if you are to hide your caper from their view.\n4\tTake a crate from the stack outside the Fox and Fiddle, in Nobottle\tThere are so many nosey hobbits around that you will need to stack crates outside the side entrance if you are to hide your caper from their view.\n5\tTalk to Dinodas Boffin on Honeymead Lane and conduct his risky caper\tDinodas Boffin is ready to begin the risky caper.\n6\tCelebrate your successful caper?\tDinodas is beaming with pride and relief after the successful execution of the caper.\n7\tTalk to Camellia Boffin beside 8 Honeymead Lane\tCamellia Boffin has discovered you! How much does she know about the recently-concluded caper?\n",
[104]="700000B5\n1\tTalk to Jarl Copperbrace\tJarl Copperbrace is in the mining-settlement of Othrikar, in the North Downs. You have received word that Jarl Copperbrace has requested the assistance of a true captain.\n2\tTalk to Jarl Copperbrace and travel to Ost Galumar\tJarl Copperbrace is in the mining-settlement of Othrikar, in the North Downs. Jarl Copperbrace is waiting to travel with you to the ruins over which he wants you to raise three standards of the Free Peoples.\n3\tBring Banners of the Free Peoples to Jarl Copperbrace\tJarl Copperbrace is in Othrikar, in the North Downs. Jarl Copperbrace is waiting to speak with you about your expedition to Ost Galumar.\n",
[105]="7006B7A3\n1\tComplete Instance: A Captive Audience\tTalk to Girhâzi when you are ready to question Khûldim Umûn again.\n2\tTalk to Girhâzi\tYou and Girhâzi succeeded in getting Khûldim Umûn to tell you where the lost archive is. You should talk to Girhâzi.\n",
[106]="7002F09F\n1\tComplete all quests for Cúfaron\030Complete all quests for Ramdir\030Complete all quests for Isteron\030Complete all quests for Maedal\tCúfaron and Ramdir are on Parth Galen. Isteron and Maedal are somewhere in the East Wall. Hestil has provided you quite the list of tasks that need to be accomplished before their guardian can be rescued from the Orcs. Help Cúfaron, Ramdir, Isteron, and Maedal, wherever they may be.\n2\tTalk to Hestil\tHestil is at her camp near Parth Galen. You have aided many members of her band and should now return to Hestil to plan the rescue of Drafli Broadshield.\n",
[107]="700453E9\n1\tExamine a carving to hear the history of the Drúedain (total: 3)\tWood carvings can be found in Drû Bhûta. Examine wood carvings to hear the history of the Drúedain.\n2\tFind a suitable piece of wood for carving\tSuitable wood for carving can be found in Taur Drúadan. Find a piece of wood for Khûr-pulo-Skâl to make a carving for you.\n3\tSpeak with Khûr-pulo-Skâl\tKhûr-pulo-Skâl can be found in Drû Bhûta. You should bring the wood to Khûr-pulo-Skâl.\n4\tFind a suitable piece of wood for carving\tSuitable wood for carving can be found in Taur Drúadan. Find a piece of wood for Khûr-pulo-Skâl to make a carving for you.\n5\tSpeak with Khûr-pulo-Skâl\tKhûr-pulo-Skâl can be found in Drû Bhûta. You should bring the wood to Khûr-pulo-Skâl.\n6\tWait for Khûr-pulo-Skâl to finish carving\tKhûr-pulo-Skâl can be found in Drû Bhûta. Wait for Khûr-pulo-Skâl to finish carving.\n7\tSpeak with Khûr-pulo-Skâl\tKhûr-pulo-Skâl can be found in Drû Bhûta. You should bring the wood to Khûr-pulo-Skâl.\n",
[108]="700413C3\n1\tReturn to the body\tThe body is located on the bank of the river Ringló, in the town of Ethring. Return to the body.\n2\tReexamine the body\tThe body is located on the bank of the river Ringló, in the town of Ethring. You should examine the body again.\n3\tSpeak with Laerind\tLaerind is located in Ethring village. You should speak with Laerind.\n4\tSpeak with Jajax\tEthring tavern is located in Ringló Vale. You should speak with Jajax.\n5\tHave a drink with Jajax\tEthring tavern is located in Ringló Vale. Have a drink with Jajax.\n6\tSpeak with Jajax\tEthring tavern is located in Ringló Vale. You should speak with Jajax.\n",
[109]="7000AE18\n1\tReturn the iron ore to Sergeant-at-Arms Gautr at Tol Ascarnen\030Collect iron ore (total: 5)\tIron ore can be found in the Isendeep Mine to the north, in Arador's End, or from the goblins of Grothum to the north-east of Tol Ascarnen. Sergeant-at-Arms Gautr at Tol Ascarnen is working to forge an iron cauldron to fill with oil to be used against the forces of Angmar as they try to retake the keep from the Free Peoples. He has asked you to help collect the iron ore needed to forge the cauldron.\n",
[110]="700195B4\n1\tDefeat Durglup\tDol Ringwest lies to the west of Duillond. Calengil wishes to drive the evil out of the ruins of Dol Ringwest. He has asked you to make your way to the ruins and seek out the goblin's leader, Durglup.\n2\tTalk to Calengil at Duillond\tCalengil is at Duillond, east of Dol Ringwest. Durglup proved a challenge for which you were well prepared. He no longer taints the ruins of Dol Ringwest. You should return to Calengil at once.\n",
[111]="7000B952\n1\tBring the wooden figurine to Tongannel\tTongannel is at Echad Candelleth, the Elf-camp in Tâl Bruinen in the Trollshaws, far to the east of Bree. Nora Strawley has given you the happy news that the body you found was not her husband -- for he survived his ordeal and made it safely back to Bree -- and has asked you to bring one of the wooden figurines to Tongannel as a sign of friendship.\n",
[112]="7000B953\n1\tBring the wooden figurines to Nora Strawley\tNora Strawley lives somewhere in the town of Bree, far to the west of the Trollshaws. Tongannel has asked you to bring the wooden figurines to Nora Strawley in the hope that she will be able to sell them and make enough coin to live on for a time.\n",
[113]="70028B83\n1\tFind the cave entrance\tThe cave entrance is believed to be in the eastern hills of Thrór's Coomb in Enedwaith. Frithgeir has translated Nár's ramblings and believes they refer to a drake-guarded cave.\n",
[114]="70020A5B\n1\tTalk to Sigismond North-took in Brockenborings\tThe Feast of the Greenfields is being held in Brockenborings in the Shire. You should speak with Sigismund North-took in Brockenborings for your introduction to the day named for the Bullroarer.\n",
[115]="70072514\n1\tListen to Malgâras's tale: Complete Celebration of Life - Glory\030Listen to Vilgerâ's tale: Complete Celebration of Life - Grace\030Listen to Dabâr's tale: Complete Celebration of Life - Folly\tPhardâli invited you to speak with others freed from the gaol-break. They wish to reward you with tales of Mûr Ghala, as they have nothing more to offer your for your noble act.\n2\tAsk Phardâli Ink-fingers about the Fool King\tHaving heard the tales and shared a night with those saved from an ignoble fate within the dungeons of Emax Dûl, you have questions for Dabâr and his tale of the blight. Speak with him at Ahâba.\n",
[116]="7006749E\n1\tReturn to Keteph at Jax Phanâl with the crab meat\030Collect chunks of delectable crab meat ([see journal]/14)\tKeteph asked you to make your way south and west of Jax Phanâl along the shore to find and collect delectable crab meat from the crabs there for a feast he means to prepare for friends and family.\n",
[117]="700226BF\n1\tTalk to Lobelia Sackville-Baggins at Bag End\tLobelia Sackville-Baggins is at Bag End, north and up the Hill from the Party Tree. You should speak with Lobelia if you are interested in getting into the newly excavated door, likely leading into a hidden cellar of Bag End.\n2\tTalk to Gaffer Gamgee on Bagshot Row\tYou seem to recall that Bilbo and Frodo, the last proprietors of Bag End, were good friends with the Gamgees on Bagshot Row, south of Bag End, just below the Party Tree. You should speak with Hamfast Gamgee, otherwise known as the Gaffer, to see if Bilbo or Frodo left him any clues as to the whereabouts of a key to the secret cellar.\n",
[118]="7000006B\n1\tTalk to Slade Ransford\tSlade Ransford is at Ost Guruth, the Ruin-hold of the Lone-lands. Slade Ransford has been asking about you, and wishes for you to speak with him about an errand of some sort.\n2\tTalk to Slade Ransford and travel with him to Ost Cyrn\tSlade Ransford is in Ost Guruth, the Ruin-hold of the Lone-lands. Slade Ransford is waiting to travel with you to Ost Cyrn to enact his plan to drive out the Orcs that have settled there.\n3\tTalk to Slade Ransford\tSlade Ransford is in Ost Guruth, the Ruin-hold of the Lone-lands. Slade Ransford is waiting for you to speak with him about the events at Ost Cyrn.\n",
[119]="700604B4\n1\tFind the Dúnadan cave\tLagordal has asked you to investigate the Dúnadan cave in the hills to the north-west.\n2\tTalk to the stranger at the Dúnadan cave\tSomeone stands in your way, blocking the entrance of the Dúnadan cave. You should talk to him.\n",
[120]="700304A1\n1\tGather extra blades of the Rohirrim (total: 6)\030Gather helms of the Rohirrim (total: 6)\tExtra arms and armour can be found scattered throughout Snowbourn and inside the Snowbourn barracks.\n2\tHaving collected arms and armour, you should now distribute it to the crofters of Snowbourn. The crofters can be found throughout the settlement.\t\n3\tTalk to Fastred\tFastred can be found in the mead-hall of Snowbourn.\n",
[121]="7004E6C2\n1\tTalk to Hórin\030Use the whistle to summon Hórin if you become separated\tYou should talk to Hórin on the path to Glimmerdeep.\n2\tDefeat Orcs on the path (total: 10)\030Use the whistle to summon Hórin if you become separated\tYou should defeat any Orcs you come across on the path to Glimmerdeep.\n3\tFind the entrance to the Glimmerdeep\030Defeat Grísblog before Glimmerdeep\030Use the whistle to summon Hórin if you become separated\tYou should search for the entranceway to the Glimmerdeep, north of Skarháld.\n4\tHelp Hórin with 'The Depth of the Problem'\030Use the whistle to summon Hórin if you become separated\tGlimmerdeep lies upon Mount Thrumfall, north of Skarháld. You should complete a full survey of the Glimmerdeep mines and whatever must be done to that end.\n5\tTalk to Hórin\030Use the whistle to summon Hórin if you become separated\tYou should talk to Hórin.\n6\tMeet Hórin at Skarháld\tYou should meet Hórin back at Skarháld.\n",
[122]="7006864E\n1\tTalk to Eshmun at the Harbour-warden's Tower\tEshmun, Captain of the Haven, can be found at the Harbour-warden's Tower in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl. Eshmun, Captain of the Haven, seeks for new guards to help safe-guard the Sail-haven in the aftermath of the Sea-stone Mutiny.\n",
[123]="7004315E\n1\tAsk Daegennan for a possible surname for Spalvi\030Ask Theodore Gorse for a possible surname for Spalvi\030Ask Thillosil for a possible surname for Spalvi\tNow that he is no longer a Dourhand, Spalvi wants a new surname, and has asked you to speak with people at Gwingris for ideas.\n2\tTalk to Spalvi at the ruins of Gwingris, in Eregion\tSpalvi is at the ruins of Gwingris, in Eregion.\n3\tSpalvi thinks that you should brainstorm ideas for his new surname as you fight the many foes in Eregion.\t\n4\tTalk to Spalvi at the ruins of Gwingris, in Eregion\tSpalvi is at the ruins of Gwingris, in Eregion. You have fought a number of enemies throughout Eregion, and should tell Spalvi the possible titles you came up with that might fit his taste.\n",
[124]="7006C58A\n1\tComplete Instance: A Changing Wind\tAmalíbi asked that you accompany her forces to confront the captain near a waystation along the road from Jirush to the Wrackwade.\n2\tTalk to Amalíbi\tYou confronted the captain and learned the Ordâkhai are splintered and near total revolt. You left the captain in the hands of Sigénik and returned to Ghalburu to speak with Amalíbi.\n",
[125]="70043B44\n1\tFind Durin's Stone by the edge of the Mirrormere, in Nanduhirion\030Defeat Orcs in Nanduhirion (total: 6)\tDurin's Stone can be found to the south-east of the exit of Moria, in Nanduhirion. Bingo wishes to see the monument Spalvi mentioned, and has asked you to defeat any of the dangers in the Dimrill Dale that threaten the peace of that place.\n2\tTalk to Bingo south-east of Durin's Stone, just beyond the falls\tBingo wants to speak with you south-east of Durin's Stone, not far from where the Mirrormere drains into a lower pool.\n3\tTalk to Bingo south-east of Durin's Stone and travel with him throughout Nanduhirion\tBingo is by the falls south-east of Durin's Stone, in Nanduhirion. Bingo is waiting for you to speak with him before you continue the journey.\n4\tTalk to Bingo outside the entrance to Caras Galadhon, in Lothlórien\tBingo is outside the entrance to Caras Galadhon, in Lothlórien. Bingo has been given permission to stay in Lothlórien for the time being, and he wishes to make the most of the opportunity.\n5\tFind Pennasseth at Cerin Nauth, in Lothlórien\tPennasseth, the Keeper of Stories, can usually be found at Cerin Nauth, on the western side of the clearing at Cerin Amroth. Bingo would like for you to find Pennasseth and borrow a book about the Elves of Lothlórien from her, so he can develop a better understanding of them.\n6\tTalk to Pennasseth at Cerin Nauth once again\tPennasseth, the Keeper of Stories, can usually be found at Cerin Nauth, on the western side of the clearing at Cerin Amroth. You obtained a book of history from Pennasseth, but she has indicated that you should not bring it back to Bingo just yet.\n7\tTalk to Pennasseth at Cerin Nauth once again\tPennasseth, the Keeper of Stories, can usually be found at Cerin Nauth, on the western side of the clearing at Cerin Amroth. You obtained a book of history and a book of maps from Pennasseth, but she has indicated that you should not bring it back to Bingo just yet.\n8\tTalk to Pennasseth at Cerin Nauth once again\tPennasseth, the Keeper of Stories, can usually be found at Cerin Nauth, on the western side of the clearing at Cerin Amroth. You obtained books of history, maps, and art from Pennasseth, but she has indicated that you should not bring it back to Bingo just yet.\n9\tReturn to Bingo outside Caras Galadhon with the stack of books\tBingo is outside the entrance to Caras Galadhon, in Lothlórien. Pennasseth, the Keeper of Stories, has given you a stack of books to give to Bingo in order to assist him with writing about the Elves.\n",
[126]="70024ECD\n1\tDonate one Yule Festival Token to Barrett Nowell\030Donate one Yule Festival Token to Ted Ives\030Donate one Yule Festival Token to Regina Judson\030Donate one Yule Festival Token to Jack Judson\030Donate one Yule Festival Token to Bill Hyde\tThe beggars can be found throughout town, and you can earn Yule Festival Tokens by participating in events at Winter-home. Inspired by Daley Utteridge's wish to be more charitable with what little he has, you should collect many Yule Festival Tokens to gift to beggars who have nothing. NOTE: This quest will consume 5 Yule Festival Tokens.\n2\tTell Daley Utteridge that he inspired you to give away your hard-earned tokens\tDaley Utteridge is in the workers' area in Winter-home. You should return to Daley Utteridge and tell him of your kindness to the beggars. You gave them your hard-earned rewards!\n",
[127]="70032BB5\n1\tLight blown-out torches\tBlown-out torches can be found near the south arch of the Twenty-first Hall. You should light the torches to stave off the chill draft.\n2\tLight blown-out torches (total: 8)\tBlown-out torches can be found near the south arch of the Twenty-first Hall. You should light the torches to stave off the chill draft.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have lit the torches in the southern section of the Twenty-first Hall that were blown out by a chill draft.\n",
[128]="7000EC2A\n1\tDefeat Ruaraikh\tRuaraikh can be found in the Angmarim encampments, south and east of Sûri-kylä, near the Ironspan in the Forodwaith pass. Pasi has asked you to defeat Ruaraikh and throw the Angmarim into disarray.\n2\tTalk to Pasi\tPasi can be found in Sûri-kylä, north and west of the Ironspan. You should return to Pasi with news of your victory.\n",
})
